X-WR-CALNAME:Marathon plan
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-23-str1-strength-legs-and-hi@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20261123T183000
DTEND:20261123T185000
SUMMARY:[RW] Strength: legs and hips (single-leg and hips) (20 min)
DESCRIPTION:Runner\, first marathon or high weekly mileage: finish healthy
 \, with limited extra training time. Lift with 2-3 reps in reserve\, stop
  a set if form breaks. Strength starts at least 3 hours after cardio (pra
 ctice).\n\nWeek 1 (BASE). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you 
 move means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-24-run1-easy-run-with-stride@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20261124T063000
DTEND:20261124T072500
SUMMARY:[RW] Easy run with strides (55 min)
DESCRIPTION:10 min warm-up\; 32 min easy\; 6 x (0.33 min hard + 1 min easy
 )\; 5 min cool-down. Six relaxed fast strides of about 20 s (RPE 7\, smoo
 th\, not a sprint) with easy jogging between. Easy means RPE 2-3: you can
  talk in full sentences. Use your watch's easy heart-rate zone if you hav
 e one.\n\nWeek 1 (BASE). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you m
 ove means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-25-bike_x-easy-ride-cross-trai@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20261125T063000
DTEND:20261125T072500
SUMMARY:[RW] Easy ride (cross-training) (55 min)
DESCRIPTION:8 min warm-up\; 42 min easy\; 5 min cool-down. Low-impact aero
 bic work next to the running: Mostly steady endurance (RPE 2-3\, 56-75 % 
 of FTP if you use power). Eat and drink on rides over 90 minutes.\n\nWeek
  1 (BASE). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you move means stop
 .\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
